A||||8||Standard||I feel so special!||||10||
Z||000000||Standard||12-06-1999||02:04 AM||||Wondering why?  I got to go to Cananda this weekend!  Of course, I was only there for about a half hour, and it was dark, and I didn't really see anything...  But I did get to talk to really bored customs officials at the border!  Me and my g/f were having a weekend getaway in Grand Marais, MN and we were bored so we decided to drive up to Canada...  Didn't see any Fieros, though.  Actually, on the 250 mile drive there and back I didn't see a single Fiero.  Kinda dissapointed me.  Did see what looked like a Lambo kit car in Duluth, though.  Nice and yellow.  Also my third whole time driving a stick... only mistake I made was shifting into second instead of fourth on an on-ramp.. Thank god for rev-limiters! scared the bejeesus out of my g/f (her car).  So yeah, I was in Canada.  Don't feel to different, tho.||||reg||10
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||12-06-1999||02:39 AM||||Guess ya weren't here long enough, eh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>hehe..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||12-06-1999||03:14 AM||||<BR>Geez, we apparently let anybody enter the country now... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||Standard||12-06-1999||04:20 AM||||I do wish that I could have stayed longer... and that it was light out... but I'll be going back up to that area this summer, so I'll be sure to spend some time in the great frozen north.  <P>Aren't they supposed to search your car at customs?  We were just asked questions by some people that looked bored out of their minds!  <P>oh yeah, and I really like the crowns on the road signs.  nice touch  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000004||batboy||12-06-1999||07:54 AM||||They only search your vehicle when you don't want them to.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Once, some athlete friends and I went up to Canada, on the way back into the U.S. the customs guy asked if we were all American. My friends said, "No, we aren't quite that good."<P>Ok, that joke probably don't make any sense to our international friends. But, to be "All American" in sports means to be the best in the country.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||12-06-1999||08:43 AM||||I remember coming back through customs after a spring break cruise to the Bahamas.  "College students to the left, everyone else can get your baggage and leave!"  Well it wasnt quite that bad, but the retired people werent having their luggage searched.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-06-1999||09:10 AM||||As I've said before in other threads, I drove a truck for 15 years.  I've been to Canada countless times and, if you are courteous and answer the questions correctly, you should never have your vehicle searched.  Just don't be a smart ass with Customs and by all means leave your weapons at home!!!  This includes that fancy new Rambo knife.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||12-06-1999||03:47 PM||||Yeah, they asked us if we had any weapons, alchohol or tabaco(sp?) products.  When they asked for a reason for our trip we had to think a little... uhhhh... sightseeing.. yeah, that's it!  Of course, the customs lady seemed a little confused when we told her we had only been in Canada for a half hour..||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||12-06-1999||08:21 PM||||The customs agents in Windsor are used to short excursions from Detroiters... the clubs and bars in Windsor are much better than their american counterparts.  Therefore, many head South to Windsor just to go out (or ouuut as the Canuks say it).  Yes those of you that are not up to speed on your geography... Windsor is South of Detroit.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
